  "text": "Twelve years. Every doctor she could pay. And Mark writes that she was \"nothing bettered, but rather grew worse.\" That is the text. Not my summary. Mark writes that she had suffered many things of many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse. Twelve years. Broke. Out of options. So she hears about Jesus. And she does not go to the front and ask. She comes up behind him in a crowd. Because she says within herself, \"If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole.\" And she does. And immediately it stops. She could have walked. That was the entire plan. Get in, get out, nobody knows. And he stops the whole procession. In a crowd pressing on him from every side, he turns around and says, \"Who touched my clothes?\" And the disciples basically tell him that is an insane question. Look at these people. He keeps looking. So she comes fearing and trembling, falls down, and tells him all the truth. Not a summary. All of it. Twelve years of it, out loud, in front of a crowd. And he says, \"Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole. Go in peace.\" Daughter. He would not let her leave as a secret.",
